## Solution

We seek the least-squares approximation (orthogonal projection) of $p(x)=x^{1/3}$ onto $W=\mathrm{span}\{1,\,x,\,x^{2}-\tfrac{1}{3}\}$ in $V=\mathcal{C}[-1,1]$ with $\langle f,g\rangle=\int_{-1}^{1}f(x)g(x)\,dx$.

### Step 1. Orthogonality of the basis

Let $e_1=1,\ e_2=x,\ e_3=x^{2}-\tfrac{1}{3}$.

- $\langle e_1,e_2\rangle=\int_{-1}^{1}x\,dx=0$ (odd integrand).
- $\langle e_1,e_3\rangle=\int_{-1}^{1}\!\bigl(x^{2}-\tfrac13\bigr)dx=\Bigl[\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}-\tfrac{x}{3}\Bigr]_{-1}^{1}=0$.
- $\langle e_2,e_3\rangle=\int_{-1}^{1}x\bigl(x^{2}-\tfrac13\bigr)dx=0$ (odd integrand).

So $\{e_1,e_2,e_3\}$ is an **orthogonal** basis of $W$. Hence the projection is

$$\mathrm{proj}_W p=\frac{\langle p,e_1\rangle}{\langle e_1,e_1\rangle}e_1+\frac{\langle p,e_2\rangle}{\langle e_2,e_2\rangle}e_2+\frac{\langle p,e_3\rangle}{\langle e_3,e_3\rangle}e_3.$$

### Step 2. Parity observation

$p(x)=x^{1/3}$ is **odd** on $[-1,1]$: $p(-x)=(-x)^{1/3}=-x^{1/3}=-p(x)$.

- $e_1=1$ is even, $e_3=x^{2}-\tfrac13$ is even, so $\langle p,e_1\rangle=\langle p,e_3\rangle=0$ (odd × even = odd, integrates to $0$ over $[-1,1]$).
- $e_2=x$ is odd, so $\langle p,e_2\rangle\neq 0$ in general.

Thus only the $e_2=x$ component survives.

### Step 3. Compute the surviving coefficient

$$\langle p,e_2\rangle=\int_{-1}^{1}x^{1/3}\cdot x\,dx=\int_{-1}^{1}x^{4/3}\,dx.$$

Since $x^{4/3}=\bigl(x^{1/3}\bigr)^{4}$ is even ($(-a)^{4/3}=a^{4/3}$),

$$\langle p,e_2\rangle=2\int_{0}^{1}x^{4/3}\,dx=2\Bigl[\tfrac{3}{7}x^{7/3}\Bigr]_{0}^{1}=2\cdot\tfrac{3}{7}=\tfrac{6}{7}.$$

$$\langle e_2,e_2\rangle=\int_{-1}^{1}x^{2}\,dx=\Bigl[\tfrac{x^{3}}{3}\Bigr]_{-1}^{1}=\tfrac{2}{3}.$$

Therefore

$$\frac{\langle p,e_2\rangle}{\langle e_2,e_2\rangle}=\frac{6/7}{2/3}=\frac{6}{7}\cdot\frac{3}{2}=\frac{9}{7}.$$

### Step 4. Assemble the approximation

$$\mathrm{proj}_W p=0\cdot 1+\frac{9}{7}\,x+0\cdot\Bigl(x^{2}-\tfrac13\Bigr)=\boxed{\dfrac{9}{7}\,x}.$$

### Verification (norm of the residual)

The residual $r=p-\tfrac97 x$ is orthogonal to $W$ by construction. As a sanity check on the coefficient, the squared error is

$$\|p\|^{2}-\frac{\langle p,e_2\rangle^{2}}{\langle e_2,e_2\rangle}=\int_{-1}^{1}x^{2/3}\,dx-\frac{(6/7)^{2}}{2/3}.$$

$\int_{-1}^{1}x^{2/3}dx=2\int_0^1 x^{2/3}dx=2\cdot\tfrac35=\tfrac65$, and $\frac{36/49}{2/3}=\tfrac{36}{49}\cdot\tfrac32=\tfrac{54}{49}$. So $\|r\|^{2}=\tfrac65-\tfrac{54}{49}=\tfrac{294-270}{245}=\tfrac{24}{245}>0$, confirming the approximation is non-trivial and the residual is genuinely orthogonal to $W$.

---

The least square approximation of $p(x)=x^{1/3}$ in $W$ is $\displaystyle \frac{9}{7}\,x$.

